.Dd August 22, 2026
.Dt XOCC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xocc
.Nd compiler wrapper for libxo's LLVM/clang plugins
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm xocc
.Ar verb
.Ar compiler-args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a small shell wrapper to aid with invoking the C compiler with
using
.Nm libxo Ns 's
LLVM plugins.
.Nm
can be used in place of
.Ev CC
in another project's build: pass it wherever that project's build
system expects a compiler, and it will invoke the real C compiler with
.Nm libxo Ns 's
plugin flags as needed.
.Nm libxo
includes LLVM/clang plugins, described in
.Xr xo_plugins 7
and xocc handles some of the details needed to invoke them properly.
.Pp
.Sh INVOKING XOCC
.Nm
requires a verb as its first argument that describe and adjusts the
actions and behaviors requested.
A verb is one or more tokens joined with
.Sq +
(enabled) or
.Sq \-
(disabled):
.Bl -tag -width "precompile"
.It Cm validate
Add the
.Nm xo_validate
plugin to the compiler invocation.
(default: disabled)
.It Cm lint
Add the extra
.Nm xo_validate
style checks
.Pq Fl \-xo\-validate\-lint ;
implies
.Cm validate .
(default: disabled)
.It Cm errors
Report the syntactic and semantic problems found by
.Nm xo_validate
as errors instead of warnings.
(default: disabled \(en i.e. warnings by default)
.It Cm precompile
Add the
.Nm xo_precompile
plugin to the compiler invocation.
(default: disabled)
.It Cm sdk
Add any configured SDK flags to the compiler invocation.
(default: enabled if the operating system needs it)
.It Cm ldflags
Add any
.Xr ld 1
flags needed for proper libxo compilation.
These are only needed (and passed) at the link stage.
(default: enabled)
.It Cm echo
Echo the command line for the underlying compiler
invocation before execution.
(default: disabled).
.El
.Pp
The token
.Cm full
is a shorthand for turning on
.Cm validate ,
.Cm lint ,
and
.Cm precompile
together.
It is a provided since this is the typical use case.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make CC='xocc full'
.Ed
Trailing "+token" / "-token" pairs adjust that starting point.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Pp
To turn warnings into hard errors, use
.Cm errors :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make CC='xocc full+errors'
.Ed
.Pp
Drop the SDK flag, or drop precompilation, the same way:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make CC='xocc full-sdk'
make CC='xocc full-precompile'
make CC='xocc full-sdk+errors'
.Ed
.Pp
Or build a verb up from nothing instead of trimming
.Cm full
down \(en these two are equivalent:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make CC='xocc validate+precompile'
make CC='xocc full-lint'
.Ed
.Pp
.Cm lint
on its own (without
.Cm validate ,
.Cm errors ,
or
.Cm precompile )
is a quick check rather than a real build:
.Nm
adds
.Fl fsyntax\-only
automatically, since there's nothing to actually compile:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make CC='xocc lint'
.Ed
.Pp
At least one of
.Cm validate ,
.Cm lint ,
.Cm errors ,
or
.Cm precompile
has to end up enabled, or
.Nm
emits an appropriate error message and exits.
.Pp
Use
.Cm echo
to see exactly what
.Nm
is about to run \(en to check a verb combination is working as expected:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make CC='xocc full+echo'
.Ed
.Pp
.Nm
picks which real compiler to invoke, but an explicit compiler can be
specified using the 
.Ev XO_REAL_CC ,
environment variable:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
XO_REAL_CC=/usr/local/bin/clang\-19 make CC='xocc full'
.Ed
.Pp
.Nm
also inspects the rest of its arguments to tell a compile stage
.Po
.Fl c ,
.Fl E ,
or
.Fl S
present
.Pc
from a link stage.
The
.Fl L Ns Ar libdir
.Fl lxo
from the
.Cm ldflags
token is only ever added at the link stage \(en
.Nm
suppresses it automatically for a compile-only invocation even if
.Cm ldflags
is on, since there's nothing to link yet:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xocc full \-c myprogram.c \-o myprogram.o
xocc full myprogram.o \-o myprogram
.Ed
.Pp
Both plugin flags, the SDK
.Fl isysroot ,
and the link flags come from values baked in when
.Nm libxo
itself was configured \(en
.Nm
needs no
.Fl I Ns Ar dir
/
.Fl L Ns Ar dir
flags pointing back at the
.Nm libxo
tree, beyond whatever the project's own build already passes for
.Nm libxo Ns 's
headers.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XO_REAL_CC
.It Ev XO_REAL_CC
Overrides the real compiler
.Nm
invokes, taking priority over the LLVM clang detected at
.Nm libxo Ns 's
configure time.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libxo 3 ,
.Xr xo_emit 3 ,
.Xr xo_options 7 ,
.Xr xo_plugins 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
wrapper first appeared in
.Fx XX.y (unknown) .
.Sh AUTHORS
.Nm libxo
was written by
.An Phil Shafer Aq Mt phil@freebsd.org .
